<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1471">1471</a>–<a href="/years/1539">1539</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as George the Bearded</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, called the Bearded, was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a> from 1500 to 1539 and a firm opponent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a>. He inherited his father Albert's rights as governor of Friesland, but faced constant revolt and war with Guelders there, and in 1515 sold Friesland to the future Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-of-saxony.jpg" alt="George of Saxony" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fotografie Albert Blanck, Leipzig · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%B6nig_Georg_von_Sachsen_in_gro%C3%9Feruniform.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
